   "worked_solution": [
      {
         "step": 1,
         "text": "The outermost operation is a product of \\( 3^{x} \\) and \\( \\tan^{2}(5x) \\), so the product rule comes first: \\( f'(x) = \\left(3^{x}\\right)'\\,\\tan^{2}(5x) + 3^{x}\\left(\\tan^{2}(5x)\\right)' \\).",
         "mathjson": [
            "Multiply",
            [
               "Power",
               3,
               "x"
            ],
            [
               "Power",
               [
                  "Tan",
                  [
                     "Multiply",
                     5,
                     "x"
                  ]
               ],
               2
            ]
         ]
      },
      {
         "step": 2,
         "text": "\\( 3^{x} \\) is an exponential function with a constant base, so its derivative is \\( 3^{x} \\ln{\\left(3 \\right)} \\); the power rule does not apply to it.",
         "mathjson": [
            "Multiply",
            [
               "Power",
               3,
               "x"
            ],
            [
               "Ln",
               3
            ]
         ]
      },
      {
         "step": 3,
         "text": "The factor \\( \\tan^{2}(5x) \\) is a square of \\( \\tan(5x) \\), which is a tangent of \\( 5x \\), so apply the chain rule from the outside inward: \\( \\left(\\tan^{2}(5x)\\right)' = 10 \\left(\\tan^{2}{\\left(5 x \\right)} + 1\\right) \\tan{\\left(5 x \\right)} \\).",
         "mathjson": [
            "Multiply",
            10,
            [
               "Add",
               [
                  "Power",
                  [
                     "Tan",
                     [
                        "Multiply",
                        5,
                        "x"
                     ]
                  ],
                  2
               ],
               1
            ],
            [
               "Tan",
               [
                  "Multiply",
                  5,
                  "x"
               ]
            ]
         ]
      },
      {
         "step": 4,
         "text": "Assemble the product rule: \\( f'(x) = 10 \\cdot 3^{x} \\left(\\tan^{2}{\\left(5 x \\right)} + 1\\right) \\tan{\\left(5 x \\right)} + 3^{x} \\ln{\\left(3 \\right)} \\tan^{2}{\\left(5 x \\right)} \\).",
